/**
\page PlanarPropertiesPage The Planar Figure Properties

The mappers of planar figures, mitk::PlanarFigureVtkMapper2D and
mitk::PlanarFigureVtkMapper3D, read these properties of a data node. Each of
them can also be set for a single render window.

| Property | Type | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| color | ColorProperty | orange (#ffaa00) | Base color. It does not change with the state of the figure; hovering and selection add a halo around it. |
| opacity | FloatProperty | 1 | Opacity of the figure. |
| line width | FloatProperty | 2 | Width of the outline in logical pixels, independent of the zoom. |
| planarfigure.drawname | BoolProperty | true | Shows the name of the node in a label next to the figure. |
| planarfigure.drawquantities | BoolProperty | true | Shows the measurements in the label, one per line. |
| planarfigure.label | PlanarFigureVisibilityProperty | On hover | When the label is shown, with the same values as planarfigure.helperlines. Figures that are helper objects or hidden objects never show a label. |
| planarfigure.drawcontrastoutline | BoolProperty | true | Draws a black outline behind light figures and a white one behind dark figures, so they stay visible on any image. |
| planarfigure.helperlines | PlanarFigureVisibilityProperty | Always, On hover for Bezier curves | When helper lines are shown: the arc of an angle, the arc and the extended lines of a four-point angle, the control polygon of a Bezier curve. Besides "Always" and "Never", they can be shown on hover, when selected, on hover or when selected, or on hover while selected; these also show them while the figure is placed. |
| font.size | IntProperty | 13 | Font size of the label in points. |
| planarfigure.3drendering | BoolProperty | false | Shows the figure in 3D render windows. |
| planarfigure.3drendering.fill | BoolProperty | false | Fills closed figures in 3D render windows. |
| animated.pulse | BoolProperty | false | Lets the figure grow and shrink by up to 8 percent. Its label stays in place. |
| animated.pulse.frequency | FloatProperty | 2 | Pulses per second. |

The 2D mapper also reads \c visible, \c selected, which adds a halo, and
\c PlanarFigureInitializedWindow: a figure of locked shape that is being placed
is shown only in the render windows where it is true, i.e. where the
interactor moves it.

Which handles are shown and how they are highlighted does not depend on
properties. mitk::PlanarFigureInteractor reports it to the mapper for the
render window under the mouse.

Scenes of previous versions carry many more properties of the previous
mapper and interactor. Loading such a scene moves \c planarfigure.line.width
to \c line \c width, \c planarfigure.annotations.font.size to \c font.size and
\c planarfigure.default.line.color to \c color, and removes the others. Values
that were the previous defaults (line width 2, font size 12, opacity 0.8,
white color) are dropped, so these figures get the current defaults, as they
do for properties added since.
*/
